      <div style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">What if I lose my TIE card?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Report the loss to local police and obtain a police report (denuncia). Present this report at the extranjería to request a replacement. The replacement card takes 1–2 weeks. Your NIE remains valid even if your physical card is lost.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">Can I use my TIE card to travel outside Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">You cannot use your TIE card as a travel document. Your TIE card is only valid in Spain. You must travel with your passport. Always carry both your passport and TIE card.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">What if my TIE card information is incorrect?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Contact the extranjería immediately to request a correction. Bring your TIE card, passport, and documentation supporting the correction. The office will issue a corrected card at no additional charge.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">Do EU/EEA citizens need a TIE card?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">EU/EEA citizens don&#x27;t require a TIE card. Instead, they must register with local authorities to obtain a Certificado de Registro de Ciudadano de la UE (EU citizen registration certificate). This serves a similar purpose but is obtained through a different process.</div>
